          "attrs": {
            "kind": "TypeDecl::AttrList",
            "loc": null,
            "children": []
          },
          "doc": "\n Regression test: a phantom type parameter in a transparent newtype wrapper\n must not make the recursion analysis treat the outer newtype as recursive.\n\n `Phantom[T]` ignores `T` — its runtime representation is just `Int` — so\n `Phantom[S]` is represented as `Int` regardless of `S`. The newtype `S` is\n therefore NOT self-referential and must unbox to a scalar `Int`.\n\n The newtype representation walk in mtype.ml must follow the *instantiated*\n underlying (`Phantom[S]` -> `Int`) rather than counting the phantom type\n argument `S`. Otherwise `S` is wrongly represented as `AnyRef` while its\n produced value is a scalar `Int`, so construction emits a `Make_newtype` that\n erases to the integer while calls/returns expect `AnyRef` — a ref-any cast on\n an integer (an ICE / miscompile). This is the phantom counterpart of\n `newtype_rec_generic_wrapper.mbt`'s used-param case.",
          "type_vis": {
            "kind": "Visibility::Default",
            "loc": null,
            "children": {}
          },
          "is_declare": false,
          "deriving": {
            "kind": "TypeDecl::DerivingList",
            "loc": null,
            "children": []
          }
        }
      }
    }
